  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV&amp;AIDS project Central Equatoria &#x2013; Sudan Aid Juba</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a 3 year project targeting the church structures at parish level in responding to the fight against HIV&amp;AIDS with the aim of increasing personal and community risk perceptions to reduce and prevent new HIV infections as well as re-infections most especially among the most at risk populations (i.e. youths, teenagers, women, etc) in all the parishes in the archdiocese in Juba and Terekeka Counties. The project targets 150 Peer Educators, 720 PLWHAs, 15 medical staff and an estimated 5,000 at risk populations who will benefit from the awareness initiatives in the parishes to be set as a result of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
